Hi Chris,

You should be able to use the stick-breaking approach to do this (see here <https://r-nimble.org/html_manual/cha-bnp.html#sec:sb> in our manual), where you'll need to specify how to construct the elements of 'v' (using the notation in the manual section) based on covariates.
I don't have an example of this, but I think it would be straightforward to translate equation 5 of Chung and Dunson into NIMBLE model code. We do have a Gaussian CDF function <https://r-nimble.org/html_manual/cha-writing-models.html#subsec:BUGS-lang-fxns> you can use in model code.

-Chris

