Hi Eduardo,

Thanks for the reproducible example you've provided off-list.

It looks like a couple things are going on here.

First, you are affected by an issue with version 1.0.0  <https://github.com/nimble-dev/nimble/issues/1324>that we discovered a week ago and are planning to fix shortly.

Second, based on your example, I see that we introduced a bug in version 1.0.0 in setting data values. (The bug came about  in the process of trying to be more careful about whether nodes that only appear on the right-hand side of an expression are flagged as 'data'.)

The bug affects models such as yours where there is a variable (`z_adt` in your case) that is a mix of data nodes and nodes that appear only on the right-hand side of expressions (or nodes that are deterministic). This would affect models such as yours that have state-space/autoregressive structure for data.

For now, please use 0.13.2 until we fix this in version 1.0.1, which I expect we will do within a few weeks (possibly sooner).

-chris

