Hi Frédéric,

Sorry about the delay in following up here. Unfortunately, I don't think changing how we refer to functions from the nimble package inside of methods such as `init_isDataEnv` will fully solve the problem (I can provide the gory details if you wish, though there are some comments in this GitHub issue <https://github.com/nimble-dev/nimble/issues/1304>). Instead, the approach we and others have taken in having packages that rely on `nimble` is to include `nimble` in `Depends` in the `DESCRIPTION` file rather than in `Imports` so that `nimble` is attached when the nimble-relying package is loaded, and therefore all objects in the nimble namespace can be found at the user level. CRAN doesn't encourage this, but it is allowed <https://cran.r-project.org/doc/manuals/R-exts.html#Package-Dependencies>.

-chris

On Tue, May 2, 2023 at 8:37 AM Chris Paciorek <paci...@stat.berkeley.edu> wrote:
> Hi Frédéric,
>
> We've often had packages that use NIMBLE have nimble in `Depends` in their DESCRIPTION, or possibly in `Imports`, with `import(nimble)` in NAMESPACE.
>
> If instead you want to use `importFrom` in NAMESPACE, which is probably when the issue would arise, I'll have to look into the scoping questions. I want to do this because it should be possible to do what you want, but I probably wouldn't get to it for a bit and not sure it would be able to be fixed for the next release.
>
> -chris
>
> On Sun, Apr 30, 2023 at 9:17 AM frederic....@gmail.com <frederic....@gmail.com> wrote:
